Let $X$ be a Banach space equipped with its norm topology $\|\cdot\|$ and an additional Hausdorff locally convex topology $\tau$, coarser than the norm topology, such that $(X,\tau)$ is sequentially complete on $\|\cdot\|$-bounded sets and the dual $(X,\tau)'$ is norming for $X$. A family $(T(t))_{t\ge 0}$ of bounded linear operators on $X$ is called a bi-continuous semigroup if:
(i) $T(0)=I$ and $T(t+s)=T(t)T(s)$ for all $t,s\ge 0$;
(ii) $(T(t))_{t\ge 0}$ is exponentially bounded in the norm of $X$;
(iii) $(T(t))_{t\ge 0}$ is locally bi-equicontinuous, i.e., for every $\|\cdot\|$-bounded $\tau$-null sequence $(x_n)$ in $X$ and every $t_0>0$, $T(t)x_n \to 0$ in $\tau$ uniformly for $t\in[0,t_0]$;
(iv) $t\mapsto T(t)x$ is $\tau$-continuous on $[0,\infty)$ for every $x\in X$.

The generator $A$ of such a semigroup is defined via the $\tau$-limit $Ax := \tau\text{-}\lim_{t\downarrow 0}(T(t)x-x)/t$ on its natural domain $D(A)$.

For strongly continuous ($C_0$) semigroups, classical regularization properties include: immediate differentiability ($T(t)X\subseteq D(A)$ for all $t>0$), immediate norm continuity, analyticity, eventual differentiability/norm-continuity, and membership in Gevrey-type classes; each is characterized by spectral/resolvent decay conditions on $A$ and by smoothing of orbits.

Formulate and establish analogous regularization notions (immediate $\tau$-differentiability, eventual $\tau$-differentiability, $\tau$-analyticity, $\tau$-Gevrey classes, immediate $\tau$-continuity, etc.) for bi-continuous semigroups, and characterize each such property in terms of the generator $A$, its resolvent, and the interplay between the norm and the topology $\tau$.

